  <static seed="214" source="Library/272/setStewart12_5/problem_16.pg">
    <statement><p>Compare the the planes below to the plane <m>2 x+ 2 y+ 5 z =
-4</m>.  Match the letter corresponding to the words parallel,
orthogonal, or "neither" which describes the relation of the two
planes.</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p><m>8 x+ 8 y+ 20 z = -2</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>2 x+ 3 y+ 5 z = -1</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>-2 x+ 2 y = -1</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
<p><ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>neither</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>parallel</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>orthogonal</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
